  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given reaction scheme, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi></math> is a phenyl alkyl ether, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Q</mi></math>&nbsp; is an aromatic compound; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> are the major products.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/d3293402-b9a3-4ebd-9210-7d978d009b19.png\" style=\"width: 580px; height: 153px;\" /></p><p>The correct statement about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi></math> is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TqMbE",
      "text": "It primarily inhibits noradrenaline degrading enzymes",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Vj898",
      "text": "It inhibits the synthesis of prostaglandin",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "n6qX7",
      "text": "It is a narcotic drug",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lauZO",
      "text": "It is ortho-acetylbenzoic acid",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The starting material&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;can be a phenol ether. When it reacts with hydrogen iodide, it gives phenol and alkyl iodide. The phenol formed undergo Kolbe&#39;s reaction with carbon dioxide in the presence of sodium hydroxide converts to salicylic acid. The salicylic acid gives Asprin on reaction with acetic anhydride.&nbsp;Aspirin&nbsp;belong to the class of non-narcotic analgesics.&nbsp;&nbsp;It&nbsp;inhibits the synthesis of prostaglandin. Antidepressant drugs are the drugs inhibit the enzymes which catalyse the degradation of noradrenaline.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/6a6929c7-c2dc-4567-b6ce-c0c10aabedf3.png\" style=\"width: 800px; height: 179px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
